  "krasnov_2026_reference": {
    "note": "Krasnov 2026 (J. Med. Chem. 69(8) 8838-8851) is a classification paper and reports its own external validation; this temporal holdout is our analogue.  No same-dataset temporal number is published there, so no numeric reference is recorded."
  },
  "why": "Close the 'external validation' metric gap: pa18 is internal DOI-grouped CV only.  A prospective temporal holdout is the strongest external validation available offline and exposes the in-distribution leakage via the random-split reference.",
  "honest_framing_note": "MEASURED only.  This is a TEMPORAL holdout, not a cross-database external set (none is available on the host with the same label rule and metal scope).  The random-split reference is a seeded diagnostic, not a second protocol.  Test active rates differ from train (recorded per metal) — that shift is the point of the axis, not a defect."
}